- a character may or may not be part of a faction
- a character can create a faction, the requirement of creating a function is provide a leader
- a faction must always have a leader
- if a faction leader dies, a member can assert leadership, of the faction memebers can vote for a new leader
- if all members of a faction die, then the faction becomes old and inactive
- a character can invite another character to join a faction
- a leader can step down as leader, leaving obligation of someone else to assert leadership or having a vote
- a character can do a coup and kill the leader and become leader
- a leader can exile members from the faction
- a faction can have any number of cities
- a faction chooses one city to be their capitol
- a character can go city and claim control of it by all faction that was controlling it
- a city can be destroyed and still owned as city-in-ruins
- a city can be abandoned by a faction
- characters can exist without factions, they do not need to be part of a faction
- a character can go to any city, if they go to a city owned by an ally you go as a friend, if you got to a neutral you are a guest, and if you go to an enemy you go as a threat or spy.
- a faction generates money for the leader to use
- a leader of a faction gives opportunities to its members. a leader can offer a charater to do spy work and provide information for the reward of money
