- faction heirarchical social structure, relative to selfishness vs selflessness

  - players with big ego assert themself in higher positions, they can be challenged to back it. the arogant ego assertion can get them in a higher position with access to more power and reources, however they will build a fragile defence about being challenged, and if it fails, then they will probably fail the competency challenge. if a honest confident character with ego is challenged, then they can back it up.
  - it is the role of mebers of the faction to be suspicious that a character is in a higher position than they should be.

